<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Surabaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1945</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesian-national-revolution">Indonesian National Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Surabaya was fought in October and November 1945 in the East Javanese port of Surabaya between Indonesian nationalist fighters and British and British Indian troops sent to accept the Japanese surrender. After the British brigadier A. W. S. Mallaby was killed, British forces launched a major assault from 10 November and took the city after weeks of fighting with heavy Indonesian losses. Its fierce resistance rallied support for the republic, and 10 November is commemorated as Heroes' Day.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-surabaya.jpg" alt="Battle of Surabaya" width="320" height="322" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sergeant Desmond Davis, No. 9 Army Film and Photographic Unit · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IWM-SE-5865-tank-Surabaya-19451127.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
